<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bashar al-Assad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1965</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bashar al-Assad was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> from 2000, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafez-al-assad">Hafez al-Assad</a>. His violent repression of the protests of 2011 led to a civil war that killed hundreds of thousands and displaced millions, in which he survived with Russian and Iranian help. In December 2024 a rebel offensive took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> and he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, ending more than fifty years of Assad rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bashar-al-assad.jpg" alt="Bashar al-Assad" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: khamenei.ir · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bashar_al-Assad_in_May_2024.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
